# P5 · Commercial launch v1.0 · Weeks 24–32 · R5 v1.0 GA
# exit: 1 first paying clinic cuts over without closing (wk 29) · 2 migration dry-run report signed before load · 3 pen test no open high/critical · 4 30 days ≥ 99.5 % availability before GA (wk 32)
# nfr:  1 RPO ≤ 15 min, RTO ≤ 4 h rehearsed · 2 99.5 % monthly availability with status page · 3 support first response < 4 business hours
# pkg:  1 signed order form + SLA · 2 migration report + go-live runbook · 3 role training (30 min each) + in-app guides · 4 v1.0 release notes
# dep:  1 regulator onboarding & conformance (UAE dates) · 2 card-reader hardware sourcing

@epic MDV-P5-E01 | Legacy migration and data quality | P5-01, P5-02 | Move a clinic's history without closing: dry run, day-one load, parallel run, backfill, fix by rule.
@epic MDV-P5-E02 | Insurance | P5-03 | Live eligibility, pre-authorisation, claims, resubmission and remittance per country.
@epic MDV-P5-E03 | UAE market pack | P5-04 | Emirates ID reader, launch-emirate exchange, regulator e-Rx and e-sick leave.
@epic MDV-P5-E04 | Outside records and voice assistant | P5-05, P5-06 | Patient uploads with verified extraction; an inbound voice booking assistant with safe handover.
@epic MDV-P5-E05 | SaaS operations | P5-07, P5-08, P5-09 | Subscriptions, platform console with audited support access, guides, status page and full data export.
@epic MDV-P5-E06 | Hardening, security operations and data rights | P5-10, P5-11, P5-12 | Pen test, DR drill, a11y audit, load test, dark/high-contrast, incident response, retention and data rights.
@epic MDV-P5-E07 | Go-live and v1.0 GA | P5-01 | First paying clinic cut-over, availability evidence and the GA gate.

=== MDV-P5-001
title: Design the 11 new P5 screens (N-04 … N-14) before build
type: Spike
epic: MDV-P5-E07
prd: P5-01, P5-02, P5-04, P5-05, P5-06, P5-07, P5-08, P5-09
screens: N-04, N-05, N-06, N-07, N-08, N-09, N-10, N-11, N-12, N-13, N-14
priority: MUST
roles: Founder, Designer
labels: design, design-needed
estimate: 4
weeks: 22-24
confidence: 60 | These screens have no designs; gap analysis gives behaviour but no layouts (PRD finding MISSING).
sources: PRD v2 findings MISSING (N-04…N-14); design/Medvya Gap Analysis
desc:
Produce lo-fi then hi-fi designs in the design project for: migration connect/mapping/dry-run (N-04), data-quality queue & bulk merge (N-05), EID reader check-in (N-06), exchange pull/push status (N-07), patient upload extraction review (N-08), letters/certificates/e-sick leave (N-09), voice assistant console & owner settings (N-10), plans/trial/subscription (N-11), platform ops console (N-12), in-app guides/help/feedback/status (N-13), clinic export (N-14). Re-import designs into design/.
ac:
- Each N-screen has an approved design with states (empty, loading, error, 403, offline) and IN/AE variants where relevant.
- Designs are imported into design/ and screen-specs updated.
- Confidence of dependent tickets is re-assessed after design (raise to ≥ 75 % where resolved).

=== MDV-P5-002
title: Migration: read-only source connection via self-hosted integration runtime (Oracle, SQL Server, MySQL, CSV/Excel) (N-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E01
prd: P5-01
screens: N-04
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations
labels: migration, data-factory
estimate: 3
weeks: 24-25
depends: MDV-P5-001
confidence: 65 | Approach defined (gap analysis Option B); every clinic's legacy schema differs.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-02 steps 1); PRD v2 P5-01
desc:
Azure Data Factory with a self-hosted integration runtime on a clinic PC (outbound only, no open ports), read-only DB user, encrypted transfer into a raw staging schema in-country. Connectors: Oracle, SQL Server, MySQL, CSV/Excel upload. Source connection registered per migration project.
ac:
- Connection requires only outbound connectivity from the clinic; no inbound firewall changes.
- The source database user is read-only (verified by attempting a write that fails).
- Raw data lands in the in-country staging area, encrypted, isolated per tenant, with retention limits.
- Connection test and inventory (tables, row counts) are shown to operations.

=== MDV-P5-003
title: Migration mapping: AI-proposed column and code mappings (LOINC, ICD-10, formulary) approved by a person; reusable vendor templates (N-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E01
prd: P5-01
screens: N-04
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Practice owner
labels: migration, mapping, ai
estimate: 4
weeks: 25-26
depends: MDV-P5-002
confidence: 62 | AI mapping quality and code-system licensing (LOINC) need validation.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-02 step 2); PRD v2 P5-01
desc:
AI proposes source→target column mappings and code mappings (local test names → LOINC, diagnoses → ICD-10, drugs → country formulary); a person approves each mapping once; approved mappings are saved as a template per legacy vendor for reuse.
ac:
- No mapping is applied without human approval; approvals are recorded with actor and time.
- Templates can be applied to a new clinic on the same vendor and diffed for changes.
- Unmapped values are listed for manual decision; nothing is silently dropped.

=== MDV-P5-004
title: Migration dry run into a test tenant and owner-signed dry-run report (N-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E01
prd: P5-01
screens: N-04
covers: exit:2, pkg:2
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Practice owner
labels: migration, report
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 26
depends: MDV-P5-003, MDV-P5-006
confidence: 72 | Report contents specified; repeatability needs careful engineering.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-02 step 3); PRD v2 P5 exit 2
desc:
Full trial load into an isolated test tenant; report: patient counts, duplicates found, records missing EID/ABHA, values failing checks, mapping coverage, sample comparisons. The owner signs the report in-app before any production load. Re-runnable any number of times.
ac:
- Production load is impossible until a dry-run report for the same mapping version is signed by the owner (exit gate 2).
- Re-running the dry run is idempotent and produces a comparable report with deltas.
- The report is exportable as PDF and stored with hash.

=== MDV-P5-005
title: Day-one load, change-data-capture parallel run and background backfill (N-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E01
prd: P5-01
screens: N-04
covers: exit:1
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations
labels: migration, cdc
estimate: 4
weeks: 27-29
depends: MDV-P5-004
confidence: 58 | CDC on clinic Oracle (Debezium/LogMiner or GoldenGate) depends on clinic infrastructure and licences.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-02 steps 4–6)
desc:
Load what day one needs (patients seen in last 24 months, future appointments, balances, active meds, allergies, problems, last results) in hours; CDC streams new legacy rows during a 1–2 week parallel run with fallback to the old system; older visits backfilled overnight in batches; scanned PDFs indexed first, OCR on open; legacy stays read-only for an agreed period.
ac:
- Day-one load completes within the agreed window with counts matching the signed dry run.
- During the parallel run, changes in the legacy system appear in Medvya within the agreed latency, without duplicates.
- Every imported value carries an "Imported" badge with source system, original id and import date.
- Cut-over checklist allows staff to fall back at any time until sign-off.

=== MDV-P5-006
title: Data-quality queue: problems grouped by type and fixed by rule; reversible (N-05)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E01
prd: P5-02
screens: N-05
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Receptionist
labels: data-quality
estimate: 3
weeks: 25-26
depends: MDV-P5-002
confidence: 65 | Behaviour defined; UI is DESIGN NEEDED.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (Making corrections fast); PRD v2 P5-02
desc:
DQ issues grouped by type (e.g. "Glucose in mg/dL stored as mmol/L", missing DOB, invalid phone); a fix rule is defined once and applied to all matching rows, then the load re-runs; each fix is reversible and audited.
ac:
- Fix-by-rule applies to all matching rows and records the rule, count and actor.
- Any rule application can be undone, restoring original values.
- Remaining issues are counted per type in the dry-run report.

=== MDV-P5-007
title: Duplicate scoring incl. Arabic–English name spellings, bulk merge for high confidence, desk confirmation for borderline (N-05)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E01
prd: P5-02
screens: N-05
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Receptionist
labels: dedup, merge
estimate: 3
weeks: 26-27
depends: MDV-P5-006, MDV-P1-017
confidence: 68 | Transliteration matching (Mohammed/Muhammad) needs tuning; merge reversibility designed in P1.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (Duplicate matching); PRD v2 P5-02
desc:
Scoring on EID/ABHA, phone, DOB and name with transliteration variants; high-confidence pairs merged in bulk (reversible); borderline pairs queued for the receptionist to confirm when the patient is at the desk. Merges audited and undoable.
ac:
- Scoring identifies seeded Arabic–English variant duplicates with documented precision/recall on the synthetic set.
- Bulk merges are reversible individually and in batch.
- Borderline pairs appear as a desk prompt on check-in for that patient.

=== MDV-P5-008
title: Insurance coverage and live eligibility with co-pay estimate at the desk (P-08)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E02
prd: P5-03
screens: P-08
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist, Practice admin
labels: insurance, eligibility
estimate: 3
