confidence: 58 | Payer APIs differ per country and need onboarding; India TPA flows are largely portal/email.
sources: design/Medvya Wireframes (P-08); design/Medvya Clinician App (insurance tab); PRD v2 P5-03
desc:
ELIGIBILITY_CHECK per coverage: live check via adapter where available (UAE platforms; India TPA where an API exists) else manual result entry with reference; shows eligible/not eligible, co-pay and validity; estimate shown to the patient. Medvya does not decide eligibility.
ac:
- Eligibility results store source, reference, timestamp and the user who checked.
- Co-pay estimate appears in billing and on the UAE portal insurance card.
- Adapter failures fall back to manual entry without blocking care.

=== MDV-P5-009
title: Pre-authorisation, claims, resubmission and remittance matching — India TPA/PMJAY/CGHS (P-14)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E02
prd: P5-03
screens: P-14
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist, Practice admin
labels: insurance, claims, india
estimate: 4
weeks: 28-29
depends: MDV-P5-008, MDV-P2-010
confidence: 65 | Form fields and claim-action list are designed; scheme-specific rules vary.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (P-14 pre-authorisation); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md
desc:
Cashless pre-auth form (patient, insurer/TPA, policy, scheme, provisional diagnosis ICD-10, proposed treatment, estimate, treating doctor) with required-documents checklist (signed note, labs, masked ID, policy card); record approval reference from TPA email/portal; claims with status; rejected/query items with reason and fix → resubmission; remittance advice matching to invoices.
ac:
- Pre-auth cannot be submitted without required documents attached.
- Claims list shows actions needed (rejected with reason, query) and resubmission history.
- Remittance matching reconciles amounts to invoices and flags short payments.
- Only signed clinical documents can be attached.

