=== MDV-P5-014
title: Patient report upload with AI extraction marked "Unverified · patient upload" until accepted (N-08)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E04
prd: P5-05
screens: N-08
priority: SHOULD
roles: Patient, Doctor
labels: uploads, ai, extraction
estimate: 3
weeks: 28-29
depends: MDV-P5-001, MDV-P3-007, MDV-P2-006
confidence: 65 | Extraction pattern exists in E-03 design; N-08 itself needs design; Document Intelligence region availability to confirm.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-01 old reports MUST); design/Medvya Clinical Screens (E-03 extracts with Confirm); PRD v2 P5-05
desc:
Patients upload PDFs/photos via portal (or WhatsApp link) before a visit; AI worker + Azure Document Intelligence extract lab values, dates and diagnoses into trend charts tagged "Unverified · patient upload"; the doctor accepts each value in one click; the original file is always kept beside the extracted values.
ac:
- Extracted values never enter verified trends until a clinician accepts them.
- Each extracted value links to the page/region of the original file.
- Uploads are malware-scanned and size/type limited; prompt-injection content in documents is ignored.

=== MDV-P5-015
title: Voice appointment assistant v1 (inbound): book/move/cancel from the live calendar, identity check, no medical advice, staff handover (N-10)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E04
prd: P5-06
screens: N-10
priority: SHOULD
roles: Patient (caller), Receptionist, Practice owner
labels: voice, ai, telephony
estimate: 6
weeks: 29-31
depends: MDV-P5-001, MDV-P1-022, MDV-P3-007
confidence: 50 | New capability with telephony (ACS + SIP trunk), multilingual speech and strict safety rules; design needed.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-06 voice appointment assistant); PRD v2 P5-06
desc:
Azure Communication Services number/SIP trunk to the clinic line; answers after hours and when lines are busy; states it is automated; identifies caller by phone then DOB or last 4 of EID/ABHA before sharing details; books/moves/cancels via the same PMS API (holds, no double booking); routine FAQs; emergency words → emergency script + immediate transfer; handover on request, after two failed attempts, complaints, billing disputes or VIPs, with transcript and summary shown to staff; reception console (listen, take over) and owner settings (hours, bookable doctors, greeting/voice, consent wording, weekly report).
ac:
- The assistant never gives medical advice, triage or results; red-team call scripts verify refusals.
- No appointment detail is disclosed before identity verification succeeds.
- Emergency phrases trigger the emergency number script and immediate transfer in every tested language.
- Bookings via voice obey the same concurrency and audit rules as reception.
- Owners can switch it on/off per branch and hour; call recording follows the configured consent wording.

=== MDV-P5-016
title: Medvya subscription: plans, trial, subscription invoices with GST/VAT, seat counts, dunning (N-11)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E05
prd: P5-07
screens: N-11
priority: MUST
roles: Practice owner, Medvya operations
labels: saas, billing
estimate: 4
weeks: 25-27
depends: MDV-P5-001, MDV-P4-001
confidence: 60 | Pricing model is an open decision (due at P4 start; default per doctor per month, AI in higher plan).
sources: PRD v2 P5-07, open decision "Pricing model"
desc:
Plans and trial (from F-01 "start free trial"), seat counting (doctors/staff), subscription invoices to clinics with GST (India) / VAT (UAE) under Medvya's own numbering, payment collection, dunning (reminders, grace period, read-only mode — never blocking access to patient records needed for care).
ac:
- Pricing decision is recorded (ADR) before implementation.
- Trial converts to paid with correct tax invoice; seat changes prorate.
- Dunning never blocks clinicians from reading existing patient records (safety rule); it limits new features/admin.
- Subscription data lives in the platform control plane with no PHI.

=== MDV-P5-017
title: Platform operations console: tenant catalogue, onboarding automation, per-tenant flags, time-boxed audited support access visible to the clinic (N-12)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E05
prd: P5-08
screens: N-12
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Practice owner
labels: platform, support, audit
estimate: 4
weeks: 26-28
depends: MDV-P5-001, MDV-P0-028
confidence: 65 | Requirements clear; design needed; support-access model must satisfy DPDP/ADHICS.
sources: PRD v2 P5-08; design/Medvya Azure Architecture (global control plane)
desc:
Ops console (separate app/role, no PHI in the control plane): tenant list per country with plan, status, flags; onboarding automation (create tenant, seed config, invite owner); support access requests that the clinic approves, time-boxed (e.g. 2 h), scoped, fully audited and visible to the clinic in its access log.
ac:
- Support staff cannot see tenant data without an approved, time-limited grant; access ends automatically.
- Every support action is audited and listed in the clinic's access log (F-12).
- Flags can be toggled per tenant from the console with audit.
- The control plane stores no PHI (data map updated).

